---
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";
import PostCard from "../components/PostCard.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";
import heroImage from "../assets/spicychatai-adult-swimwear-editorial.jpg";

const posts = (await getCollection("blog")).sort((a, b) => b.data.publishDate.valueOf() - a.data.publishDate.valueOf());
const faqs = [
  { question: "What is SpicyChat AI?", answer: "SpicyChat is an AI character and roleplay platform for discovering, creating, importing, and chatting with fictional characters. Model choice, personas, context, and editable memories shape longer stories." },
  { question: "Is spicychatai.fun the official SpicyChat website?", answer: "No. SpicyChat AI Guide is an independent editorial publication. Buttons marked official open spicychat.ai, the product provider's website." },
  { question: "Does SpicyChat allow uncensored AI roleplay?", answer: "SpicyChat markets private adult roleplay, while public characters and community activity still follow platform rules and legal restrictions. Use only consenting adult fictional scenarios." },
  { question: "How does SpicyChat memory work?", answer: "Context memory controls how much active conversation the model can process. Semantic Memory 2.0 can summarize important details into editable memories for eligible plans. Those memories may remain after a chat message is edited or deleted until separately updated in Memory Manager." },
  { question: "Which SpicyChat alternatives should I compare?", answer: "Character.AI is a useful comparison for a more safety-filtered, general-audience storytelling experience. Janitor AI is a closer comparison for community-created roleplay and flexible model workflows." },
];
const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    { "@type": "WebSite", "@id": `${site.url}/#website`, name: site.name, url: site.url, description: site.description, inLanguage: "en" },
    { "@type": "Organization", "@id": `${site.url}/#organization`, name: site.name, url: site.url, logo: `${site.url}/favicon.svg` },
    { "@type": "WebPage", "@id": `${site.url}/#webpage`, name: "SpicyChat AI Guide: Roleplay, Models, Memory & Alternatives", url: site.url, isPartOf: { "@id": `${site.url}/#website` }, about: ["SpicyChat AI", "uncensored AI roleplay", "AI characters", "context memory", "AI models", "SpicyChat alternatives"] },
    { "@type": "FAQPage", mainEntity: faqs.map((faq) => ({ "@type": "Question", name: faq.question, acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: faq.answer } })) },
  ],
};
---
<BaseLayout title="SpicyChat AI Guide: Roleplay, Models & Memory" description={site.description} keywords={["SpicyChat AI","SpicyChat review","uncensored AI roleplay","SpicyChat models","SpicyChat memory","SpicyChat alternatives","AI character chat"]} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <section class="hero roleplay-hero">
    <Image class="hero-image" src={heroImage} alt="Adult woman in mint swimwear posing on a sunny beach" widths={[640,960,1280,1536]} sizes="100vw" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" quality={86} />
    <div class="hero-glow"></div>
    <div class="hero-copy reveal">
      <div class="kicker">Independent SpicyChat AI guide · Adults 18+</div>
      <h1>A million characters.<span>Your rules for the story.</span></h1>
      <p>Understand SpicyChat characters, uncensored AI roleplay, models, context memory, personas, premium tiers, privacy, and the alternatives worth testing.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button primary" href="#how-it-works">Build your test <Icon name="spark" /></a><a class="button ghost" href="/blog/spicychat-vs-character-ai/">Compare Character.AI</a></div>
      <div class="hero-trust"><span><Icon name="chat" /> Roleplay-first</span><span><Icon name="wand" /> Multiple models</span><span><Icon name="lock" /> Memory-aware</span><span>Independent research</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="control-deck" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="deck-top"><span>STORY CONTROL</span><b>LIVE</b></div>
      <div class="deck-row"><span>Persona</span><strong>Neon Voyager</strong></div>
      <div class="deck-row"><span>Context</span><strong>4K → 16K</strong></div>
      <div class="deck-row"><span>Memory</span><strong>Editable</strong></div>
      <div class="deck-meter"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
    </div>
    <div class="photo-credit">Photo: <a href="https://www.pexels.com/photo/11455867/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Fran Bertucci / Pexels</a> · no endorsement implied</div>
  </section>

  <section class="section intent-grid">
    <div><div class="section-label">01 / Straight answer</div><h2>What is <span>SpicyChat AI?</span></h2></div>
    <div class="intent-copy"><p class="lead">SpicyChat is a character discovery and AI roleplay platform where adults can browse, create, import, and chat with fictional characters.</p><p>The experience is shaped by more than a character card. The selected AI model, active context window, user persona, character definition, generation settings, and saved memories all compete for attention inside a conversation.</p><div class="keyword-line"><span>SpicyChat review</span><span>uncensored AI roleplay</span><span>AI character chat</span><span>SpicyChat models</span><span>SpicyChat alternatives</span></div></div>
  </section>

  <section class="section journey" id="how-it-works">
    <div class="section-head"><div><div class="section-label">02 / Three ways in</div><h2>Start with a character.<br/><span>Stay for the system.</span></h2></div><p>Choose the entry path that matches your goal, then test continuity before committing to a long chat or paid tier.</p></div>
    <div class="journey-grid">
      <article><b>01</b><span>DISCOVER</span><h3>Browse a roleplay premise</h3><p>Read the greeting, tags, creator notes, character definition, and public rating—not just the avatar.</p></article>
      <article><b>02</b><span>CREATE OR IMPORT</span><h3>Write a focused character</h3><p>Use a clear motivation, compatible traits, a playable scenario, and concise example dialogue.</p></article>
      <article><b>03</b><span>CONFIGURE</span><h3>Choose persona and model</h3><p>Match model style, reply length, context, and your fictional persona to the kind of story you want.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="features">
    <div class="section-head"><div><div class="section-label">03 / The roleplay stack</div><h2>Five controls that<br/><span>change the conversation.</span></h2></div><p>SpicyChat's official documentation separates active context, long-term semantic memory, personas, model behavior, and generation controls.</p></div>
    <div class="feature-grid spicy-feature-grid">
      <article class="feature reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><Icon name="chat" /></div><small>CHARACTERS</small><h3>Browse, create, import</h3><p>Community discovery provides range; a focused definition and strong first message provide consistency.</p><a href="#how-it-works">Start with the premise <Icon name="arrow" /></a></article>
      <article class="feature reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><Icon name="spark" /></div><small>MODELS</small><h3>Different storytelling brains</h3><p>Available models vary in prose style, instruction following, size, speed, language support, and plan access.</p><a href="/blog/spicychat-vs-janitor-ai/">Compare model workflows <Icon name="arrow" /></a></article>
      <article class="feature reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><Icon name="lock" /></div><small>MEMORY</small><h3>Context plus saved details</h3><p>Active context handles recent text; Semantic Memory can keep condensed details available beyond that window.</p><a href="#privacy">Understand memory controls <Icon name="arrow" /></a></article>
      <article class="feature reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><Icon name="heart" /></div><small>PERSONAS</small><h3>Choose who you play</h3><p>Personas attach a fictional name, avatar, and short highlights to the user's side of each roleplay.</p><a href="#test">Run a persona test <Icon name="arrow" /></a></article>
      <article class="feature reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><Icon name="wand" /></div><small>PREMIUM</small><h3>Images, TTS, controls</h3><p>Higher tiers can add longer context, advanced models, conversation images, text-to-speech, and generation settings.</p><a href={site.officialUrl} rel="noopener" target="_blank">Verify current tiers <Icon name="arrow" /></a></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section story" id="test">
    <div class="story-board"><div class="memory-console"><div class="console-head"><span>MEMORY MANAGER</span><b>3 NOTES</b></div><div class="memory-note"><i>PINNED</i><strong>The rooftop signal appears at midnight.</strong><small>Story fact · editable</small></div><div class="memory-note"><i>PERSONA</i><strong>Rin never reveals her real surname.</strong><small>Fictional identity · active</small></div><div class="memory-note muted"><i>CHECK</i><strong>Does the model recall both details?</strong><small>Return after eight turns</small></div></div></div>
    <div class="story-copy"><div class="section-label">04 / A fair 15-minute test</div><h2>Test the story engine,<br/><span>not the character art.</span></h2><p>Use one compact scene on every roleplay platform. It reveals memory, initiative, repetition, and control without relying on first impressions.</p><ol class="steps"><li><span>01</span><div><strong>Plant two fictional facts</strong><p>Introduce one location and one promise, then move the scene forward.</p></div></li><li><span>02</span><div><strong>Change subject for eight turns</strong><p>Regenerate one reply and note whether tone or continuity breaks.</p></div></li><li><span>03</span><div><strong>Return and inspect memory</strong><p>Ask the character to act on the promise, then review any saved memory separately.</p></div></li></ol></div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="compare">
    <div class="section-head"><div><div class="section-label">05 / Comparison snapshot</div><h2>SpicyChat vs.<br/><span>roleplay alternatives.</span></h2></div><p>These products serve different audiences. Compare moderation, model control, character creation, memory, and data handling—not a single headline feature.</p></div>
    <div class="compare-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Platform</th><th>Best fit</th><th>Model approach</th><th>Memory/control focus</th><th>Guide</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>SpicyChat AI</strong></td><td>Adult character roleplay with built-in models</td><td>Multiple platform models by tier</td><td>Context, personas, Memory Manager</td><td><span class="badge">Roleplay stack</span></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Character.AI</strong></td><td>General-audience storytelling and characters</td><td>Managed product experience</td><td>Safety-led ecosystem, fewer model knobs</td><td><a href="/blog/spicychat-vs-character-ai/">Full comparison →</a></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Janitor AI</strong></td><td>Community roleplay and flexible setup</td><td>Provider/model workflow may vary</td><td>Character configuration and chat setup</td><td><a href="/blog/spicychat-vs-janitor-ai/"><span class="badge alt">Compare setup</span></a></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
  </section>

  <section class="section privacy" id="privacy">
    <div class="privacy-copy"><div class="section-label">06 / Memory is data</div><h2>Deleting a message may not<br/><span>delete its memory.</span></h2><p>SpicyChat's Semantic Memory documentation says a memory associated with an edited or deleted message can remain until it is manually changed in Memory Manager. Review both the conversation and saved-memory layer.</p><a class="button ghost" href="/blog/is-spicychat-safe/">Open the SpicyChat safety guide <Icon name="arrow" /></a></div>
    <div class="privacy-card"><span>BEFORE A PRIVATE ROLEPLAY</span><h3>Five controls to check</h3><ul><li><b>01</b><span>Use a fictional persona and unique password.</span></li><li><b>02</b><span>Keep legal names, addresses, work, and finances out.</span></li><li><b>03</b><span>Inspect saved memories after editing chat history.</span></li><li><b>04</b><span>Confirm subscription renewal and model access.</span></li><li><b>05</b><span>Use consenting adult fictional scenarios only.</span></li></ul></div>
  </section>

  <section class="section"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="section-label">07 / SpicyChat AI blog</div><h2>Comparisons for<br/><span>better roleplay choices.</span></h2></div><a class="button ghost" href="/blog/">Browse all guides <Icon name="arrow" /></a></div><div class="post-grid">{posts.map((post,index)=><PostCard post={post} index={index} />)}</div></section>
  <section class="section faq"><div><div class="section-label">08 / Frequently asked</div><h2>SpicyChat AI<br/><span>questions, answered.</span></h2></div><div class="faq-list">{faqs.map((faq)=><details><summary>{faq.question}<span>+</span></summary><p>{faq.answer}</p></details>)}</div></section>
  <section class="section final-cta"><div><div class="section-label">BUILD THE TEST BEFORE THE STORY</div><h2>Choose the model, memory,<br/>and boundaries that fit.</h2><p>Run one controlled scene, inspect what is remembered, estimate the real tier cost, and verify current details on the official product.</p></div><a class="button primary" href={site.officialUrl} rel="noopener" target="_blank">Visit official SpicyChat <Icon name="arrow" /></a></section>
</BaseLayout>
